From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: validate cached L2 output before reuse

DIRECT software output bypasses neighbor and root-bridge forwarding
after initial admission. Retain its native neighbor and bridge path
signature so a changed neighbor, FDB destination or bridge VLAN policy
tears down the old flow before rewriting another packet. VLAN and
PPPoE upper devices retain their normal lower forwarding ownership.

Delayed hardware REPLACE also needs current source authority: DIRECT
rules copy cached Ethernet addresses and NEIGH rules sample them while
building actions. Validate those identities again through a borrowed
synchronous callback; the provider owns ordinary teardown on mismatch.
Drivers can place the check inside their notifier admission interval
without retaining flowtable objects or interpreting private cookies.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
---

--- a/include/net/flow_offload.h
+++ b/include/net/flow_offload.h
@@ -695,6 +695,11 @@
 	bool use_act_stats;
 	unsigned long cookie;
 	struct flow_rule *rule;
+	/* Optional source admission check for this synchronous REPLACE call.
+	 * Neither callback nor borrowed context may be retained by a driver.
+	 */
+	bool (*validate)(void *priv);
+	void *validate_priv;
 	struct flow_stats stats;
 	u32 classid;
 };
